# move-dumper

TypeScript tool. Simulates match play between skill levels and dumps labelled positions from [foochu/bgweb-api](https://github.com/foochu/bgweb-api).

- Loop, pairing, levels: `docs/domain/move-dumper.md`. Match loop from `ts-core/sim`. Match math: `docs/domain/match-play.md`. Board helpers come from `ts-core`.
- Convert at the boundary per `docs/domain/gnubg.md`. Store our JSON + evals only. Rank chosen checker plays by mover MWC.
- On-disk batches: `docs/domain/dump-format.md` under `move-dumper/dumps/` (`manifest.json` + `records.jsonl.gz` + `replay/*.sgf`).
- Do not call the gnubg CLI for labels. Never commit `dumps/`. Fixtures in `move-dumper/fixtures/` may be committed.
- Docker only, from `move-dumper/`: `npm run up` (teacher), `npm test`, `npm run dump -- …`, `npm run down`. `npm run install:host` writes `node_modules` on the host for IDE typechecking; do not run dumps or tests from that tree. Do not run `dump:inner` / `test:inner` on the host.
